# an-orchestrator-that-fails

Alice's closure, where one of the ORCHESTRATOR's units of work does not commit: the saga row 
it advanced and the records it produced go together, so a rollback leaves the confirmation 
it was reading where it was and a death after the commit loses them, because that loop sends 
straight to the broker and marks the saga once the send is proven. One sweep is left, so the 
recovery those records have instead of a relay — the next sweep re-issuing them — is in the 
tree as well. The question is whether the case can be made to finish twice, or to finish and 
forget that it did. 

